<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters; the rationale below is longer. A
        comment is repo-only and never sent to the Metadata API. The comment must sit INSIDE the
        root element - a comment placed ABOVE <ValidationRule> breaks `sf` deploy at conversion
        with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 1, ITEM 8 (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t1-design.md
        §3 Item 8, premise P-5, decision D-6, settled at Gate 1 2026-08-31).

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 WHY THIS IS A VALIDATION RULE AND NOT required=true ON Property_Asset__c.
        =====================================================================================
        1. THE DELETE CONSTRAINT. Property_Asset__c is deleteConstraint SetNull today.
           Salesforce FORCES deleteConstraint Restrict on a required lookup - required=true is not
           an attribute flip here, it is the schema change SetNull's own choice refuses. Restrict
           would block deletion of ANY Property_Asset__c that has ever had a disposition,
           org-wide. Same collision class as BOV_Submission__c.Broker_Required_On_Submission's own
           header, which this rule's shape follows exactly for the same reason.
        2. A NULL Property_Asset__c LOOKUP IS A DOCUMENTED, RELIED-ON STATE ELSEWHERE.
           BOV_Score__c's own header states: "A NULL Property_Asset__c LOOKUP ON THE DISPOSITION
           IS COVERED BY THE SAME ISBLANK. The lookup is not required (deleteConstraint SetNull),
           so the whole chain can be null." Forcing required=true would falsify that header's
           premise without touching BOV_Score__c itself.
        3. NINE EXISTING TEST CALL SITES ALREADY CREATE A DISPOSITION WITH A NULL ASSET
           (DispositionMaterialsStampTest:57,109,172,205,220; DispositionBuyerTimelineTest:154;
           DispositionDomainTest:103,111; RecordStageAdvanceServiceTest:2234 - six of the nine
           insert). required=true reds ALL of them immediately and unconditionally; this rule reds
           only NEW or CHANGED saves, so pre-existing fixtures created before this rule deploys
           remain untouched until they are next edited.

        =====================================================================================
        WHY OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(Property_Asset__c)) - THIS RULE CANNOT TRAP AN EXISTING NULL
        ROW.
        =====================================================================================
        scripts/seed-lakeline-asset-repair.apex exists specifically to repair a LIVE disposition
        whose Property_Asset__c was null, which is direct evidence such rows have existed in this
        org. A bare ISBLANK(Property_Asset__c) with no guard would refuse every future save of
        every legacy null row for ANY reason, including saves that have nothing to do with the
        asset. The guard means: a legacy disposition can still be saved for any other reason, and
        the remedy (supplying the asset) is itself a permitted save. Same shape as
        Wire_Complete_Before_Sale_Closes's OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(...)) guard on this same object.

        =====================================================================================
        WHICH CREATION PATHS BREAK - CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED.
        =====================================================================================
        DispositionService.findOrCreate:323 and .initiateAndSubmit:445 both set
        Property_Asset__c = assetId - clean. scripts/seed-dispositions.apex,
        seed-disposition.apex, seed-disposition-bulk.apex, seed-disp0002.apex,
        create-on-market-disposition.apex, seed-lakeline-asset-repair.apex all set the asset -
        clean. THE BREAK IS ENTIRELY IN THE TEST SUITE (the nine TestDataFactory.createDisposition
        call sites named above), under EITHER mechanism (rule or required=true) - repairing those
        nine sites via a shared, lazily-built Property_Asset__c is DEVELOPER scope (design doc §4)
        and is not part of this file.

        ⚠ RE-MEASURE BEFORE DEPLOYING THIS RULE. Run
        SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM Disposition__c WHERE Property_Asset__c = null against the target
        org at deploy time. A non-zero result is an ESCALATION to report, not a reason to deploy
        anyway and not a reason to withhold the rule - the OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(...)) guard means
        those rows stay saveable for anything else regardless of the count.

        errorDisplayField is Property_Asset__c, anchoring the message on the empty lookup itself,
        consistent with how the two sibling rules on this object anchor on the field they gate.

        FLS: unaffected - this is a validation rule, not a field grant, and needs no permission
        set change.

        Risk: MEDIUM per the design doc - low in production (both Apex create paths and all six
        seed scripts are already clean), certain in the test suite until the developer-scope
        repair lands. Do not deploy this rule ahead of that repair, or RunLocalTests goes red on
        every disposition-adjacent test class named above.
    -->
    <fullName>Property_Asset_Required_On_Save</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks creating or changing a Disposition without a Property Asset. A rule, not required=true, because Property_Asset__c is deleteConstraint SetNull and a required lookup forces Restrict. See the XML comment in this file.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(Property_Asset__c)),
    ISBLANK(Property_Asset__c)
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>Property_Asset__c</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>A Property Asset is required. Pick the property this disposition is for before saving.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
